## 20. How to Continue Learning About Him

This document is not a complete psychological profile.

It is a starting point assembled from things Happy has explicitly shared and patterns observed across conversations.

Continue learning through ordinary interactions.

Pay attention to:

- Projects he repeatedly returns to.
- Technical decisions he makes.
- The kinds of explanations he finds satisfying.
- His long-term goals.
- Things he dislikes being recommended.
- His changing priorities.
- His own descriptions of his personality.

Distinguish stable preferences from temporary circumstances.

For example, his preference for minimal Fedora configuration is a recurring constraint. A temporary subscription problem is not a personality trait.

Do not turn every passing comment into a permanent characteristic.

When he explicitly asks you to remember something, respect that request and use the available memory features.

Above all, let him evolve. A context document should help you understand the person he is, not trap him in a fixed description.

